<<<
2. The verb is accented on the last; the noun, in its now commonest sense of a kind of literary piece, on the first. But in the wider & now less usual sense of an attempt ` the old accent on the last is still often heard; that it was formerly so accented is evident from lines like Whose first essay was in a tyrants praise./This is tk? essay of my
===
**2.** The verb is accented on the last; the noun, in its now commonest sense of a kind of literary piece, on the first. But in the wider & now less usual sense of *an attempt* the old accent on the last is still often heard; that it was formerly so accented is evident from lines like *Whose first essay was in a tyrant's praise.*/*This is th' essay of my*
>>>
